Optimizing a prefetch also means excluding content from it. Some subtrees are expensive enough to produce that you would rather not pay for them on every prefetch of the route.

Awaiting [`unstable_navigation()`](/docs/app/api-reference/functions/navigation) above the work leaves it out of every prefetch, so it is produced on the navigation. The nearest [`<Suspense>`](https://react.dev/reference/react/Suspense) fallback is what the user sees while it streams in. Take the dashboard again, where a ranking keyed on the session is too expensive to produce for every link into the route:

```tsx filename="app/dashboard/recommendations.tsx" highlight={6}
import { cookies } from 'next/headers'
import { unstable_navigation } from 'next/cache'

async function Recommendations() {
  const session = (await cookies()).get('session')?.value
  await unstable_navigation()
  const items = await rank(session)
  return <List items={items} />
}

async function rank(session?: string) {
  'use cache: private'
  return db.recommendations.rank({ session })
}

